survivors: measured sessions join without a savepoint

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recorded 2026-10-07. The survivor is EQUIVALENT, not a gap. Without
join_transaction_mode="create_savepoint", SQLAlchemy 2.0's default
("conservative_savepoint") joins the outer transaction in rollback-only mode:
a session's commit is not propagated, so nothing reaches the store and every
later session sees the earlier writes. The two modes differ only when a session
inside the pass rolls back and the pass then continues -- under the default that
rollback would undo the whole outer transaction mid-pass. The pass never does
that: every failure propagates and the transaction is rolled back at the end.
Result: 17 of 17 non-equivalent mutants killed. The setting is kept as the
statement of intent and the guard for that future case.
